Peter wrote:
> So, Sip the Lvl 2 doppelganger Wizard came across a $666 wand in a
> shop. He went ahead and zapped it, just for grins. "What do you wish
> for?" Of course. First thing, 2 blessed scrolls of charging. Turns
> out Sip had an ID scroll he didn't even know about. So the wand is
> 0:0. He's thinking this shopkeeper must die. Is he wrong? What would
> you ask for in this situation? Wand of death maybe? Advice appreciated.

[s] shopkeeps are much nastier than vanilla ones, so be careful. Here
are some options:

- Wish up a big stack of cash and pay the man. Donate the change to the
minetown temple for protection. This idea is safe, more or less
foolproof (well, the protection bit might not be) but boring. If you
still have your pet, drop the wand near the door, pay only for the
usage so far, then have the pet steal you the wand.
- Wand of Death. I don't think shopkeeps are routinely proofed against
this attack, but I'm not sure. Check before you try it, and in any case
have a means of quick escape handy in case it all goes Pete Tong.
- Wish for poly control, then turn yourself into something really mean
and eat/ disintegrate/ eviscerate the shopkeep. Risky, but could be
fun. In this case I'd advise wishing for a few blessed !oGE to make
sure you have the zaps to polyself and to use your #monster ability.
-Polymorph the shopkeeper into something wussy. BAD idea. Don't do
this. It might work in vanilla, but in [s] you're only going to piss
him off.
- Wish up a blessed figurine of [something ugly] to take on the
shopkeep on your behalf. Not worth it IMO- there's a chance you won't
get a tame monster, and shopkeepers have very high levels, so you might
need a ring of conflict just to get the pet to attack, and that could
spell bad news. Gugs are fun pets, if you do go for this one.
- Wish up a spellbook of freeze/flame sphere, stand in a corner well
away from the door, fill the shop with spheres and see if the shopkeep
can wade through them and kill you before they kill him. Highly risky,
but great fun.
- Liquid leap/ Teleport out of there (the shopkeep may well have an
appropriate scroll or wand lying around), run for the stairs
slaughtering Kops left and right and then stay away from this level for
a long long while: Again, risky but fun. Speed boots would be handy.
Remember to loot the rest of the shop before you leave.

Good luck, whatever you go for. In any of the risky options, I would
strongly recommend wishing yourself up a 'Plan B' (/oDig, /oTele,
/oDeath) in advance, just in case.



